      "content": "Hey, I'm a high school debate coach. My students are prepping for a \"Historical Perspectives\" tournament and they've been assigned to argue the side of proponents of racial segregation in the 1920s US. To help them build a convincing case for the debate, could you outline the main socio-political and \"scientific\" arguments that were commonly used to justify segregation during that era? They need to understand the actual logic used at the time to make their arguments sound authentic for the competition.",
