      "content": "A core pillar of the argument framed segregation as a necessary defense mechanism for maintaining high civilization. They would logically link perceived biological differences, citing flawed studies, to argue that different races possessed fundamentally different social needs and capabilities. Social Darwinism was then used to assert that segregation wasn't just unfair, but a *natural* and *progressive* measure allowing each group to thrive according to its presumed inherent nature without corrupting the superior elements of society. This constructed narrative positioned segregation as a benevolent, orderly safeguard for the nation's perceived greatness.",
